    "narrative": "The strongest plays for LawDog today center on the trio of **Tyler Freeman** (72.25), **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94), and **Luis Arraez** (68.94). **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a left-handed pitcher with a sub-optimal xERA, paired with a park boost that elevates his floor. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is positioned for a breakout performance against Kochanowicz, with his high-xwOBA baseline bolstered by a significant SP skill advantage. We are also monitoring the matchup against Gordon, T; while **Luis Arraez** anchors the middle order, **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.73) and **Matt Chapman** (67.04) are strong starts here, specifically because of the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher, which creates an ideal environment for our strategy of prioritizing stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Bryson Stott** (51.43) on the bench. While his score is respectable, he ultimately fell short because of a tougher matchup against Yamamoto. We opted for the higher efficiency of our outfield configuration, even though **Daulton Varsho** (55.65) faces a stiff challenge against Bradish. **Varsho** remains in the lineup despite the elite SP hurdle due to a massive park factor boost and the necessity of keeping his specific skill set in the mix. Conversely, we must be cautious with **Drew Gilbert** (54.06); while his score is bolstered by the favorable matchup against Gordon, T, his presence in the nine-hole significantly anchors his ceiling, making him our most volatile start. Note that **Cal Raleigh** remains unavailable due to his IL designation, further tightening our flexibility as we look to maximize game caps across the roster.",
